# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MintVault code ownership
#
# GitHub requests a review from the listed owner on any pull request touching a
# matching path. Combined with branch protection this makes the frozen grading
# ruleset impossible to change without the owner seeing it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# MVGS v1.4 — IMMUTABLE GRADING RULESET
#
# These paths determine how ~700 issued certificates — and the physical slabs
# printed from them — were graded. They are frozen by SHA-256 in
# mvgs-v1_4-freeze.manifest.json and by golden vectors in
# tests/mvgs-v14-golden-vectors.test.ts.
#
# A pull request touching any of them will fail CI at the freeze gate.
# That is intended. To change how cards grade, add shared/mvgs/v1_5/ instead.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
/shared/mvgs/                          @mintvaultuk-byte
/shared/mvgs-scoring.ts                @mintvaultuk-byte
/shared/centering.ts                   @mintvaultuk-byte
/shared/pristine.ts                    @mintvaultuk-byte
/shared/mvgs-input-builder.ts          @mintvaultuk-byte
/shared/grade-presentation.ts          @mintvaultuk-byte
/server/lib/draft-grade-authority.ts   @mintvaultuk-byte
/server/lib/grade-kind.ts              @mintvaultuk-byte
/mvgs-v1_4-freeze.manifest.json        @mintvaultuk-byte
/scripts/mvgs/                         @mintvaultuk-byte
/tests/fixtures/mvgs-v1_4-golden.json  @mintvaultuk-byte
/tests/mvgs-v14-freeze.test.ts         @mintvaultuk-byte
/tests/mvgs-v14-golden-vectors.test.ts @mintvaultuk-byte

# The published standard is the customer-facing statement of those same rules.
/client/src/pages/standard.tsx         @mintvaultuk-byte

# Payments and auth remain owner-reviewed for the same reason: consequence.
/server/stripeClient.ts                @mintvaultuk-byte
/migrations/                           @mintvaultuk-byte
